  data: {
    LLM: "Strategy is simpler than it looks. You should play (bet 1x) if you have any pair of 10s or better. If you have less than 10s, you should fold.\n\nThe 3x Bet: Whenever you have a Pair of Aces or better (including any Three-of-a-Kind), you should always bet the maximum (3x). The statistical advantage on these hands is too large to ignore.\n\nDealer Upcard Analysis: If the dealer's visible face-up card is higher than your best card, and you only have a low pair (e.g. 2s or 3s), consider folding even if you 'should' play by the 10s rule, as the dealer has 5 other chances to beat you.",
